      "duplicates": 0,
      "lastReply": "Here is your story: Sheru and the biryani.\n\nDeep in the Sundarbans lived a tiger named Sheru who was tired of the same raw dinner every night. One evening a warm, spicy smell drifted over from a village wedding, and he followed it to a giant pot of biryani. He hid behind a banyan tree, watched the old cook layer rice and masala, and decided he would learn to make it himself.\n\nHis first attempts were a mess. He burnt the rice, dumped in a whole fistful of chillies and sneezed so hard that the monkeys fell out of their trees laughing. But Sheru kept at it. He crept back every night to watch the cook, learnt to fry the onions golden, to add saffron and mint, and to seal the pot and wait, which was the hardest part for a hungry tiger.\n\nAt last, one full-moon night, he lifted the lid and the whole jungle went quiet at the smell. The deer, the monkeys and even the grumpy old crocodile came to taste it, and nobody was afraid of him any more. From then on Sheru was known not as the fiercest tiger in the forest but as its finest cook, and every full moon was biryani night. 🐯\n\n9:46 AM",
